                <pb facs="0778" n="764" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v1/pg764"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Seward, Secretary of State, to Mr. McCulloch,
                        Secretary of the Treasury.</hi>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1866-05-09"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 9,
                        1866</date>.</dateline>
                <p><seg type="margin">[12]</seg>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In a note of this day, Mr. Tassara, the
                    Spanish minister, says that he has information that a vessel named the Panoa, or
                    Pocus, will start from New London to-night or to-morrow as a privateer against
                    Spain. Pursuant to his request, I will consequently thank you to telegraph to
                    the collector of customs at that place *to detain the vessel for examination, if
                    in his judgment there should be sufficient cause therefor.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">H. McCulloch</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of the Treasury.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
